  "body": "The vendors are committed to their next move and are keen to achieve a result. All genuine offers will be given serious consideration, so don't hesitate to put forward your interest.\r\n\r\nPositioned in one of Army Bays most peaceful and sought-after streets, this impressive four-bedroom home captures stunning views across Shakespear Regional Park, Okoromai Bay and the Hauraki Gulf. This vast home offers a wonderful sense of space, privacy, and tranquillity.\r\nSolidly built from brick and weatherboard and with its versatile layout, beautiful outdoor entertaining and spectacular swimming pool, this is a property you really must see.\r\n\r\nStep inside and discover a home designed for comfortable family living, entertaining and flexibility.\r\nUpstairs, the spacious master bedroom is a private retreat, complete with a luxurious ensuite and a large walk-in wardrobe. It has its own private deck looking out to Rangitoto Island. Also on this level are two further double bedrooms and a large modern family bathroom, making this ideal for everyday family life.\r\nThe heart of the home is the large open plan living and dining area, complemented by a functional, modern family kitchen. Whether you're enjoying a quiet morning coffee while taking in the view or entertaining friends and family, this space is designed to make the most of the home's incredible setting.\r\n\r\nAnd then there's the separate second lounge, providing plenty of room for movie nights, teenagers, guests, hobbies or simply spreading out and relaxing.\r\nDownstairs, the very spacious fourth bedroom with its own ensuite and walk in robe offers fantastic flexibility. This is an ideal arrangement for extended family, a boarder, visiting guests or a teenager wanting their own private space and independence.\r\nOutside, the lifestyle continues.\r\nThe large, well-maintained, fully-fenced garden provides plenty of room for children, pets and entertaining, while the stunning in-ground swimming pool is sure to become a favourite gathering place throughout the warmer months. The home has solar panels which saves on power, particularly in Summer. There is plenty of storage, off-street parking and a double garage with the laundry.\r\n\r\nEnjoy easy access to the beach and Shakespear Regional Park, with the Gulf Harbour ferry just a short drive away for convenient access to Auckland city. It's a peaceful coastal setting that offers the perfect balance of relaxed living, recreation, and connectivity.\r\n\r\nDon't miss your opportunity to secure this exceptional Army Bay property. Call Sarah today for more information or come along to a scheduled open home.\r\n\r\nConjunctionals with other agencies are welcome.\r\n\r\nTo view/download files please copy this link into your browser: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/YIIZ",
